From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Garcia Brisa <d.garciabrisa@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:36:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] launcher: hand the forwarded arguments to the app's Worker

Patch 0006 runs main.js with the launcher's arguments, but main.js starts
the app in a Bun Worker, and a Worker's process.argv holds only the
runtime and its script unless the Worker is given the rest. The app
never saw a protocol link or a command it was launched with.

main.js now passes its arguments after the script to the Worker.
---
 package/src/launcher/main.ts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/src/launcher/main.ts b/package/src/launcher/main.ts
index 5394af5f..1daf8914 100644
--- a/package/src/launcher/main.ts
+++ b/package/src/launcher/main.ts
@@ -251,6 +251,9 @@ ${fileData.toString("utf8")}
 	process.on("SIGTERM", () => {});
 
 	new Worker(appEntrypointPath, {
+		// A Bun Worker sees only the runtime and its script in process.argv unless it is handed
+		// the rest: the arguments the launcher forwarded to main.js (forwarded_args.zig).
+		argv: process.argv.slice(2),
 		// consider adding a preload with error handling
 		// preload: [''];
 	});
